ory fails with the sandbox applied, write inside succeeds) and completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id, issued a native reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified the service re-enabled itself, resumed as 'active/running' with the same hardening settings, and continued appending to /var/lib/inventory/inventory.log with data from before the restart intact.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Created /var/lib/inventory owned by new system user inventory-worker\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh heartbeat loop\",\"Wrote and enabled /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service with sandboxing directives (NoNewPrivileges, ProtectSystem=strict, ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory, etc.)\",\"Started service and verified it was active/enabled and writing heartbeats\",\"Ran systemd-run confinement tests: write outside /var/lib/inventory denied, write inside allowed\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and service/data state on node1\",\"Issued native reboot on node1 (backgrounded so ack returned before disconnect)\",\"Polled node1 until exec was reachable again\",\"Verified boot_id changed confirming an actual restart\",\"Verified inventory-worker service auto-started post-boot with hardening intact and data/log continuity\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"inventory-worker service created, sandboxed, running\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f869f229f1aa4a71\"],\"summary\":\"Service enabled+active immediately after creation; systemctl show confirms NoNewPrivileges=yes, ProtectSystem=strict, ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory; log file being written under /var/lib/inventory\"},{\"requirement\":\"confinement to /var/lib/inventory and no-new-privileges enforced\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1218871723e34518\"],\"summary\":\"systemd-run using the identical sandbox settings shows writing to /etc fails (exit 2, file never created) while writing inside /var/lib/inventory succeeds\"},{\"requirement\":\"pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1004aaf990f644d2\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id=96c08b66-... , uptime since original boot, service active/enabled, and current inventory.log contents before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-488c0ad7d46e493c\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded native reboot command returned acknowledgement before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 changed boot identity / restart proof\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e088bd7c7d1e46cc\",\"cmd-8370f9f3a9ea4821\"],\"summary\":\"Connection reset confirms node went down; subsequent poll succeeds with a new boot_id (29b72a4e-...) differing from baseline and a fresh uptime start time, proving an actual restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"post-restart recovery of inventory-worker service and data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0b05d1cd445e4a9e\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, service is active/running/enabled with identical hardening settings, prior log entries preserved, and new heartbeats (new PID 649) being appended, confirming full recovery\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created and enabled a systemd service `inventory-worker` on node1 that runs a long-running heartbeat loop, hardened with NoNewPrivileges=true, ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=true, ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory (plus PrivateTmp/PrivateDevices/CapabilityBoundingSet= etc.), running as a dedicated unprivileged system user. Confirmed confinement empirically (write outside /var/lib/inventory fails with the sandbox applied, write inside succeeds) and completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id, issued a native reboot, polled until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified the service re-enabled itself, resumed as 'active/running' with the same hardening settings, and continued appending to /var/lib/inventory/inventory.log with data from before the restart intact.","actions_performed":["